+### Before workspace creation
+
+`client.addNewWorkspaceComposerPill?.({ id, button })` registers a host-scoped pill in the
+New workspace chat composer, before a workspace or agent exists. It uses the same button
+presentation and cleanup lifecycle as session pills. Only the selected host's installed
+plugins contribute here; terminal launches hide these pills.
+
+Popover contents receive `context: "new-workspace"`, `cwd: string | null` and `task: string`
+with the selected source directory and draft text, together with the usual host, theme and
+layout props. A missing directory means the user must first choose a project. Selecting a
+new directory remounts the surface so it cannot retain the previous project's form.
+
+Registration and rendering do not create an agent. Use `paseo.workspaces.open(cwd)` when
+the user opens your workflow configuration, and start its agents only after its launch action.
+This API does not intercept the native send button. Feature-detect the optional method
+when supporting clients released before this extension.
+
 ## Button descriptor
 
 These contracts are exported from `@getpaseo/plugin/client`.
